- `void sa/sb/sc(game_t *game)` - Swap operations
- `void pa/pb(game_t *game)` - Push operations  
- `void ra/rb/rr(game_t *game)` - Rotate operations
- `void rra/rrb/rrr(game_t *game)` - Reverse rotate operations
- `void choose_sort_algorithm(game_t *game)` - Main sorting dispatcher
- `int list_is_sorted(list_t *list)` - Sorting verification

## Data Structures
### List Node:
```c
typedef struct list_s {
    int value;           // Integer value
    struct list_s *next; // Next node pointer
} list_t;
```

### Game State:
```c
typedef struct game_s {
    list_t *l_a;        // Stack A
    list_t *l_b;        // Stack B  
    char **operations;   // Operation history
    int op_count;       // Number of operations
    int op_capacity;    // Operation array capacity
} game_t;
```

